CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ argument array destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ array destroyed after initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ vector elements destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed: the backing array, held in a static-lifetime symbol
(initializer_list_backing_array) whose elements are constructed in place,
is now a temporary of its full-expression in goto conversion (clean_expr)
and destroyed at its end, unless an initializer_list variable is
initialized from it (cpp11_initializer_list_elements_destroyed_with_the_
array).  Assertion 3 also needed std::_Destroy's header body
(cpp11_vector_destroys_its_elements).
